### Authentication API Test File
### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/auth

### Variables
@token = 

### Note: Before testing login, you need to create a user in the database.
### You can use H2 console at http://localhost:8080/h2-console
### Or insert via SQL: INSERT INTO users (username, email, password) VALUES ('testuser', 'test@example.com', '$2a$10$...');
### Password should be BCrypt encoded. Use: https://bcrypt-generator.com/ with rounds=10
### Example: password "password123" -> $2a$10$N9qo8uLOickgx2ZMRZoMyeIjZAgcfl7p92ldGxad68LJZdL17lhWy

### 1. Login with valid credentials
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Login with invalid password (should fail with 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 3. Login with non-existent user (should fail with 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "nonexistent",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 4. Login with empty username (should fail with 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 5. Login with empty password (should fail with 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "password": ""
}

